# IntestacyCascade — AEA 1925 s.46 cascade + LPA 1925 s.184 / AEA 1925 s.46(2A) commorientes

The full intestacy distribution cascade on death without a valid will (Administration
of Estates Act 1925 s.46, as amended, most recently by the Inheritance and Trustees'
Powers Act 2014) plus the survivorship gate that decides who is treated as having
survived the intestate for the purposes of that cascade (Law of Property Act 1925
s.184 general commorientes presumption; AEA 1925 s.46(2A) spouse-specific 28-day
survival period, which displaces s.184 for the intestate's spouse or civil partner).

Legal correctness is asserted **outside this file** by the T032 per-heir gov-oracle
harness (TT-463 pattern): `code-inherit-test-suite/scripts/oracle_verify.py` runs the
`Distribute` scope, reads `per_member_amounts`, expands each element by the matching
`member_counts` integer into the per-heir multiset, and compares it against
`tests/oracles/intestacy-cascade-aea1925.oracle.json` — including a committed
`wrong_split` negative fixture that must turn the harness RED if a right-sum/
wrong-split answer ever matched. This file therefore carries the division law, not
its own per-heir assertions.

(Prose note: a line must not begin with the reserved `>` directive prefix, so any
statutory quotation is kept inline.)

**Both scopes live in this one module** because clerk 1.2.0 does not resolve
cross-module `output of Mod.Scope` calls (TT-478 finding) — only intra-module
`output of Scope` does. `Distribute` does not itself call `Survivorship`; it takes
the survival outcome as a **boolean** input, `spouse_survives_statutory_period`,
because the T032 per-heir harness can only render boolean/list/money case inputs (an
integer `days_survived` would emit an unrenderable `$28` literal). The day-based
28-day arithmetic is therefore isolated in `Survivorship` and proven separately by
the in-file `#[test]` scopes below.

**G6 certification floor (TT-427/TT-1079).** Every `Distribute` input is a
characterisation judgement (who is a spouse, who counts as issue, what the estate is
worth — see `registry/governance-layers.yaml`, all L3), so each is declared with the
matching `ComputedOrNeedsHuman.Certified<Type>` enum, not a bare scalar. A caller must
certify each characterisation or the scope routes `NeedsHuman` — `uncertified_inputs`
below is the typed gate; the `_v` internals unwrap certified values and are only
meaningful under `not uncertified_inputs` (every output is guarded). `Survivorship`
stays bare-scalar: it returns no Verdict — its conclusion re-enters this boundary as
the certified `spouse_survives_statutory_period`.

## Survivorship — LPA 1925 s.184 / AEA 1925 s.46(2A)

Verbatim, LPA 1925 s.184: "In all cases where ... two or more persons have died in
circumstances rendering it uncertain which of them survived the other or others,
such deaths shall (subject to any order of the court), for all purposes affecting
the title to property, be presumed to have occurred in order of seniority, and
accordingly the younger shall be deemed to have survived the elder." Verbatim, AEA
1925 s.46(2A): "Where the intestate's spouse or civil partner survived the intestate
but died before the end of the period of 28 days beginning with the day on which the
intestate died, this section shall have effect as respects the intestate as if the
spouse or civil partner had not survived the intestate." The 28-day rule applies to
the intestate's spouse or civil partner regardless of whether the order of the two
deaths was itself uncertain, and displaces the s.184 seniority presumption for that
spouse. `days_survived` is the number of clear days the claimant survived the
intestate; the boundary is `>= 28` because the period is 28 days beginning with the
day of death.

```catala
declaration scope Survivorship:
  input is_spouse_of_intestate content boolean
  input days_survived content integer
  input order_uncertain content boolean
  input claimant_is_elder content boolean
  input actually_survived content boolean
  context survival_period_days content integer
  output treated_as_surviving content boolean

scope Survivorship:
  definition survival_period_days equals 28
  definition treated_as_surviving equals
    if is_spouse_of_intestate then
      # AEA 1925 s.46(2A): the intestate's spouse/civil partner is treated as
      # having survived the intestate only if they in fact survive by the
      # statutory 28-day period. This displaces the s.184 presumption for the
      # spouse, whether or not the order of the two deaths was itself uncertain.
      days_survived >= survival_period_days
    else
      # LPA 1925 s.184: where the order of two deaths is uncertain, the elder
      # is presumed to have died first, so the elder does NOT survive and the
      # younger does. Where the order is certain, actual survival governs
      # (even survival by under a day counts).
      if order_uncertain then (not claimant_is_elder)
      else actually_survived
```

## Distribute — the s.46 cascade

Statutory class order (AEA 1925 s.46(1), current in-force text, verified against
legislation.gov.uk on `sourced_at` in the oracle): **(i)** spouse/civil partner —
Table Case (1) no issue: spouse takes the whole residuary estate absolutely (post
Inheritance and Trustees' Powers Act 2014, parents/siblings no longer share); Table
Case (2) has issue: (A) spouse takes personal chattels absolutely, (B) the residuary
estate other than chattels is charged with the fixed net sum (the statutory legacy)
plus interest to the spouse, (C) subject to (B) the remaining residuary estate other
than chattels is held as to one half for the spouse absolutely and the other half on
the s.47 statutory trusts for the issue; **(ii)** issue but no spouse: the whole
residuary estate on the s.47 statutory trusts for the issue; **(iii)** no spouse, no
issue, both parents: the father and mother in equal shares absolutely; **(iv)** no
spouse, no issue, one parent: that parent absolutely (not exercised by a distinct
oracle case — it is the two-code-path degenerate of the s.46(1)(v) "winning class"
mechanism used for siblings/grandparents/uncles-aunts below, and is out of MVP
oracle scope per the Global Constraints); **(v)** no spouse, no issue, no parent: in
order — First, whole-blood siblings (s.47 statutory trusts); Secondly, half-blood
siblings (s.47 statutory trusts); Thirdly, grandparents in equal shares; Fourthly,
whole-blood uncles/aunts (s.47 statutory trusts); Fifthly, half-blood uncles/aunts
(s.47 statutory trusts); **(vi)** default: Crown / Duchy of Lancaster / Duke of
Cornwall as bona vacantia — discretionary Treasury Solicitor territory, routed to
`NeedsHuman`, never computed as a split.

The statutory legacy (fixed net sum) and the 28-day survival period are `context`
parameters with overridable literal defaults (ICP-A1 discipline): `statutory_legacy`
defaults to £322,000, confirmed as the amount in force from 26 July 2023 by SI
2023/758 (the Administration of Estates Act 1925 (Fixed Net Sum) Order 2023, raising
it from £270,000); `survival_period_days` (on `Survivorship` above) defaults to 28.

MVP scope boundary: `net_estate` is the residuary estate available for distribution
after debts and funeral expenses; `chattels_value` is the personal chattels, which
the spouse takes on top when the spouse takes under (i), and which fold into the
distributable fund whenever the spouse does not take (chattels are a distinct
statutory category ONLY under s.46(1)(i)(A), which applies solely where a spouse
survives — s.46(1)(ii)-(vi) direct "the residuary estate" with no separate chattels
carve-out). No RNRB/IHT interaction (`IhtDeathCharge` owns taxation, this scope owns
distribution). The statutory legacy's interest (s.46(1)(i)(B) — the fixed net sum
carries interest from death until payment/appropriation) is out of MVP scope: the
split is computed as at the date of death, no interest accrual. No partial
intestacy, no s.33 express-trust interplay, no minority-contingency accumulation —
those route to `NeedsHuman`. The fixed net sum is clamped to the estate: where
`net_estate` is smaller than `statutory_legacy`, the spouse cannot receive more than
exists, so the spouse takes the whole (smaller) estate and the issue take nothing
(the statute does not explicitly spell out this case, but it follows directly from
s.46(1)(i)(B) charging the fixed net sum "against" a residuary estate that cannot pay
more than it holds).

```catala
declaration scope Distribute:
  input net_estate content ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney
  input chattels_value content ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney
  input spouse_present content ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool
  input spouse_survives_statutory_period content ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool
  input has_issue content ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool
  input issue_branch_sizes content ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedIntegerList
  input winning_class_branch_sizes content ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedIntegerList
  input winning_class_per_stirpes content ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool
  input winning_class_is_crown content ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool
  input member_counts content ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedIntegerList
  context statutory_legacy content money
  internal uncertified_inputs content boolean
  internal net_estate_v content money
  internal chattels_value_v content money
  internal spouse_present_v content boolean
  internal spouse_survives_statutory_period_v content boolean
  internal has_issue_v content boolean
  internal issue_branch_sizes_v content list of integer
  internal winning_class_branch_sizes_v content list of integer
  internal winning_class_per_stirpes_v content boolean
  internal winning_class_is_crown_v content boolean
  internal spouse_survives content boolean
  internal effective_legacy content money
  internal residue content money
  internal no_eligible_relative content boolean
  internal needs_human content boolean
  internal distributable_no_spouse content money
  output per_member_amounts content list of money
  output total_distributed content money
  output verdict content ComputedOrNeedsHuman.Verdict

scope Distribute:
  definition statutory_legacy equals $322,000
  # G6 typed gate: ANY uncertified characterisation routes the whole scope to
  # NeedsHuman (member_counts included — it has no _v because no definition
  # below reads it; it exists for the per-heir harness).
  definition uncertified_inputs equals
    (match net_estate with pattern -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney.Certified content v: false -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney.NotCharacterised: true)
    or (match chattels_value with pattern -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney.Certified content v: false -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney.NotCharacterised: true)
    or (match spouse_present with pattern -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content v: false -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.NotCharacterised: true)
    or (match spouse_survives_statutory_period with pattern -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content v: false -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.NotCharacterised: true)
    or (match has_issue with pattern -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content v: false -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.NotCharacterised: true)
    or (match issue_branch_sizes with pattern -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedIntegerList.Certified content v: false -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedIntegerList.NotCharacterised: true)
    or (match winning_class_branch_sizes with pattern -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedIntegerList.Certified content v: false -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedIntegerList.NotCharacterised: true)
    or (match winning_class_per_stirpes with pattern -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content v: false -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.NotCharacterised: true)
    or (match winning_class_is_crown with pattern -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content v: false -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.NotCharacterised: true)
    or (match member_counts with pattern -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedIntegerList.Certified content v: false -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedIntegerList.NotCharacterised: true)
  # certified-value extractions — the NotCharacterised fallbacks are DEAD CODE:
  # every consumer definition is guarded by uncertified_inputs above
  definition net_estate_v equals
    match net_estate with pattern -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney.Certified content v: v -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney.NotCharacterised: $0
  definition chattels_value_v equals
    match chattels_value with pattern -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney.Certified content v: v -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney.NotCharacterised: $0
  definition spouse_present_v equals
    match spouse_present with pattern -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content v: v -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.NotCharacterised: false
  definition spouse_survives_statutory_period_v equals
    match spouse_survives_statutory_period with pattern -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content v: v -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.NotCharacterised: false
  definition has_issue_v equals
    match has_issue with pattern -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content v: v -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.NotCharacterised: false
  definition issue_branch_sizes_v equals
    match issue_branch_sizes with pattern -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedIntegerList.Certified content v: v -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedIntegerList.NotCharacterised: []
  definition winning_class_branch_sizes_v equals
    match winning_class_branch_sizes with pattern -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedIntegerList.Certified content v: v -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedIntegerList.NotCharacterised: []
  definition winning_class_per_stirpes_v equals
    match winning_class_per_stirpes with pattern -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content v: v -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.NotCharacterised: false
  definition winning_class_is_crown_v equals
    match winning_class_is_crown with pattern -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content v: v -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.NotCharacterised: false
  definition spouse_survives equals spouse_present_v and spouse_survives_statutory_period_v
  # the fixed net sum cannot exceed the estate that exists to pay it
  definition effective_legacy equals
    if net_estate_v < statutory_legacy then net_estate_v else statutory_legacy
  definition residue equals
    if net_estate_v - statutory_legacy > $0 then net_estate_v - statutory_legacy else $0
  # chattels are only a distinct category under s.46(1)(i)(A) (spouse takes);
  # otherwise they remain part of "the residuary estate" passed to the class
  definition distributable_no_spouse equals net_estate_v + chattels_value_v
  # no computable taker: Crown/bona vacantia (s.46(1)(vi)) OR no eligible
  # relative in any class (empty winning class with no spouse and no issue)
  definition no_eligible_relative equals
    (not spouse_survives) and (not has_issue_v) and (number of winning_class_branch_sizes_v = 0)
  definition needs_human equals winning_class_is_crown_v or no_eligible_relative
  definition per_member_amounts equals
    if uncertified_inputs or needs_human then []
    else if spouse_survives and has_issue_v then
      # s.46(1)(i) Table Case (2): (A) chattels + (B) clamped fixed net sum to
      # the spouse; (C) the remaining residue split half spouse absolutely /
      # half to the issue on the s.47 statutory trusts (per stirpes)
      (let issue_fund equals residue * 0.5 in
       let n equals number of issue_branch_sizes_v in
       let branch_share equals (if n > 0 then issue_fund * (1.0 / (decimal of n)) else $0) in
       [chattels_value_v + effective_legacy + residue * 0.5]
         ++ (map each b among issue_branch_sizes_v to (branch_share * (1.0 / (decimal of b)))))
    else if spouse_survives and (not has_issue_v) then
      # s.46(1)(i) Table Case (1): no issue, spouse takes the whole estate
      [chattels_value_v + net_estate_v]
    else if has_issue_v then
      # s.46(1)(ii): issue but no spouse, whole (chattels-inclusive) estate
      # on the s.47 statutory trusts per stirpes
      (let n equals number of issue_branch_sizes_v in
       let branch_share equals distributable_no_spouse * (1.0 / (decimal of n)) in
       map each b among issue_branch_sizes_v to (branch_share * (1.0 / (decimal of b))))
    else
      # s.46(1)(iii)-(v): no spouse, no issue — the winning class (parents /
      # whole-blood siblings / half-blood siblings / grandparents / uncles-
      # aunts) takes the whole estate, per stirpes or equally per the flag.
      # winning_class is non-empty here (empty routed to needs_human above).
      (let n equals number of winning_class_branch_sizes_v in
       let branch_share equals distributable_no_spouse * (1.0 / (decimal of n)) in
       if winning_class_per_stirpes_v
       then map each b among winning_class_branch_sizes_v to (branch_share * (1.0 / (decimal of b)))
       else map each b among winning_class_branch_sizes_v to branch_share)
  # NOT `sum money of per_member_amounts`: that list holds the PER-MEMBER
  # (already-divided) share for each branch, so naively summing it undercounts
  # any branch with more than one member (e.g. a predeceased sibling's two
  # children) — it would add one member's share instead of the whole branch's.
  # Each arm below reconstructs the true total from the pre-division amounts,
  # which conserve by construction regardless of branch membership.
  definition total_distributed equals
    if uncertified_inputs or needs_human then $0
    else if spouse_survives and has_issue_v then chattels_value_v + effective_legacy + residue
    else if spouse_survives and (not has_issue_v) then chattels_value_v + net_estate_v
    else distributable_no_spouse
  definition verdict equals
    if uncertified_inputs then NeedsHuman
    else if needs_human then NeedsHuman
    else Computed content total_distributed
```

## In-file tests — the day-based boundary and the NeedsHuman branch

The per-heir harness cannot render an integer `days_survived`, so the 28/27-day
boundary is proven here instead; likewise `NeedsHuman` carries no split for the
harness to assert, so it is proven here too.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestSurvivorship28:
  output result content boolean

scope TestSurvivorship28:
  definition result equals
    (output of Survivorship with {
      -- is_spouse_of_intestate: true
      -- days_survived: 28
      -- order_uncertain: false
      -- claimant_is_elder: false
      -- actually_survived: true
    }).treated_as_surviving
  assertion result = true

#[test]
declaration scope TestSurvivorship27:
  output result content boolean

scope TestSurvivorship27:
  definition result equals
    (output of Survivorship with {
      -- is_spouse_of_intestate: true
      -- days_survived: 27
      -- order_uncertain: false
      -- claimant_is_elder: false
      -- actually_survived: true
    }).treated_as_surviving
  assertion result = false

#[test]
declaration scope TestSurvivorshipS184:
  output result content boolean

scope TestSurvivorshipS184:
  definition result equals
    (output of Survivorship with {
      -- is_spouse_of_intestate: false
      -- days_survived: 0
      -- order_uncertain: true
      -- claimant_is_elder: true
      -- actually_survived: false
    }).treated_as_surviving
  assertion result = false

#[test]
declaration scope TestCrownNeedsHuman:
  output is_needs_human content boolean
  output member_count content integer

scope TestCrownNeedsHuman:
  definition is_needs_human equals
    match (output of Distribute with {
      -- net_estate: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney.Certified content $100,000
      -- chattels_value: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney.Certified content $0
      -- spouse_present: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content false
      -- spouse_survives_statutory_period: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content false
      -- has_issue: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content false
      -- issue_branch_sizes: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedIntegerList.Certified content []
      -- winning_class_branch_sizes: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedIntegerList.Certified content []
      -- winning_class_per_stirpes: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content false
      -- winning_class_is_crown: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content true
      -- member_counts: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedIntegerList.Certified content []
    }).verdict with pattern
    -- Computed content m: false
    -- NeedsHuman: true
  definition member_count equals
    number of (output of Distribute with {
      -- net_estate: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney.Certified content $100,000
      -- chattels_value: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney.Certified content $0
      -- spouse_present: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content false
      -- spouse_survives_statutory_period: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content false
      -- has_issue: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content false
      -- issue_branch_sizes: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedIntegerList.Certified content []
      -- winning_class_branch_sizes: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedIntegerList.Certified content []
      -- winning_class_per_stirpes: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content false
      -- winning_class_is_crown: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content true
      -- member_counts: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedIntegerList.Certified content []
    }).per_member_amounts
  assertion is_needs_human = true
  assertion member_count = 0

#[test]
declaration scope TestUncertifiedRoutesNeedsHuman:
  output routed content boolean
  output member_count content integer

scope TestUncertifiedRoutesNeedsHuman:
  # G6 (TT-1079): ONE uncertified characterisation (here the estate valuation)
  # routes the whole cascade to NeedsHuman — no number is reachable, and the
  # sibling outputs are neutral ([] / $0), never a meaning-bearing figure.
  definition routed equals
    match (output of Distribute with {
      -- net_estate: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney.NotCharacterised
      -- chattels_value: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney.Certified content $0
      -- spouse_present: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content true
      -- spouse_survives_statutory_period: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content true
      -- has_issue: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content false
      -- issue_branch_sizes: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedIntegerList.Certified content []
      -- winning_class_branch_sizes: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedIntegerList.Certified content []
      -- winning_class_per_stirpes: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content false
      -- winning_class_is_crown: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content false
      -- member_counts: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedIntegerList.Certified content []
    }).verdict with pattern
    -- Computed content m: false
    -- NeedsHuman: true
  definition member_count equals
    number of (output of Distribute with {
      -- net_estate: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney.NotCharacterised
      -- chattels_value: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney.Certified content $0
      -- spouse_present: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content true
      -- spouse_survives_statutory_period: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content true
      -- has_issue: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content false
      -- issue_branch_sizes: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedIntegerList.Certified content []
      -- winning_class_branch_sizes: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedIntegerList.Certified content []
      -- winning_class_per_stirpes: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content false
      -- winning_class_is_crown: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content false
      -- member_counts: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedIntegerList.Certified content []
    }).per_member_amounts
  assertion routed = true
  assertion member_count = 0
```
